86045417] [17592186544749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544749 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544749 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544749 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544749 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186544106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544749 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cdcd0ddb-26c1-5d8a-bd2b-b23dc08e9c29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186544596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544770 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "edd2fc28-bb7b-522b-8b22-9cd25ae03847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544783 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544783 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75336" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544783 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544783 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[3,13]\\times [3,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=12{x}^{2}+19{y}^{2}+3.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544783 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04a3375f-8916-5fd6-a307-59704d7589ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544783 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=12{x}^{2}+19{y}^{2}+3$ increases as $x$ increases on $[3,13],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=12{x}^{2}+19{y}^{2}+3$ increases as $y$ increases on $[3,7].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=12{x}_{i}^{2}+19{y}_{j}^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(12{x}_{i}^{2}+19{y}_{j}^{2}+3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $12{x}_{i}^{2}+19{y}_{j}^{2}+3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544822 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544822 #edb/ref 1069 "q-170684" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544822 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544822 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-1,3]\\times [-4,-2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=8y-2x-5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544822 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5cf5fafd-606c-53b3-9dcd-de496f0b8804" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544822 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=8y-2x-5$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=8y-2x-5$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/74/74d546d91e145efea49b70af56cb472e8bbbd1417725cd7fa92a3a278cad75ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}-5)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544827 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544827 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75335" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544827 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544827 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[3,4]\\times [1,9]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}-21.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544827 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "673e501d-d4fb-5f61-85b5-c2fe793fdded" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544827 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}-21$ increases as $x$ increases on $[3,4],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}-21$ increases as $y$ increases on $[1,9].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=3{x}_{i}^{2}+8{y}_{j}^{2}-21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}^{2}+8{y}_{j}^{2}-21)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}^{2}+8{y}_{j}^{2}-21.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544851 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544851 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544851 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544851 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=30-7{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544851 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99966b73-9392-5920-a350-678f41228cda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544851 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partiti